  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to Follow the Numbered Flow (Steps 1 -> 8)",
      "items": [
        "Steps 1-3 (Condition & Authorize): Repo AGENTS.md conditions the AI Coding Assistant (1), which calls the deterministic MCP Server :8000 (2) to verify project_id permissions and sync state in the Central DB (3)",
        "Step 4 (Modular SDLC/STLC Agents): MCP Server dispatches any individual LangGraph agent or custom sequence (Backlog/AC, QA Test Matrix, Spec Scaffolding, Validation Guard)",
        "Steps 5-8 (100% LLM Governance): Both the Coding Assistant and all 4 Agents route LLM calls through Portkey :8787 (5), enforcing DLP/RBAC hooks (6), Redis quotas (7), and multi-cloud failover (8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Service Observability: MCP + All 4 Agents -> Loki + Grafana",
      "items": [
        "AgenticGuard MCP Server AND all 4 LangGraph Agents ship structured service logs via their embedded Fluentbit library to Loki (:3100) and Grafana (:3001)",
        "Tracks MCP access-control rejections, DLP hook triggers, and container health without blocking the request hot path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "AI Observability: All 4 Agents -> Langfuse (:3000)",
      "items": [
        "All 4 LangGraph Agents connect directly to Langfuse (:3000) via CallbackHandler to record multi-step agent traces, prompt versions, and validation rubric scores",
        "Correlates token spend with first-pass PR validation rates across Cursor, Claude Code, and Codex"
      ]
    }
  ]
